1) This is the right syntax for creating an if statement in Python:
if (condition):
2) In this case, the condition is the expression that must evaluate as true before the block of code within the parentheses is executed. In your example, this is the condition (i < 3). If the condition evaluates to false, the code within the parentheses will not be executed.

